## Log-Based Verification

Verify recovery through log analysis:

```typescript
// 1. Compare logs before and after fixes
run_terminal_cmd("Get-Content -Path \"logs-main/front-end/$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd').log\" -Tail 50", false)

// 2. Check for specific error resolution
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path \"logs-main\" -Recurse -Filter \"*.log\" | Select-String -Pattern \"[previous_error_pattern]\" | Measure-Object | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Count", false)

// 3. Create verification documentation
edit_file("[planning_folder_path]/log-verification-results.md",
          "Document log-based verification",
          "# Log-Based Verification Results\n\n## Error Pattern Analysis\n\n| Error Pattern | Before Fix Count | After Fix Count |\n|--------------|-----------------|----------------|\n| [pattern_1] | [count] | 0 |\n| [pattern_2] | [count] | 0 |\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n| Component | Before Render Time | After Render Time | Improvement |\n|-----------|-------------------|-------------------|-------------|\n| [component_1] | [time]ms | [time]ms | [percentage]% |\n\n## Log Evidence\n\nBefore fix:\n```\n[log snippet before fix]\n```\n\nAfter fix:\n```\n[log snippet after fix]\n```")
```

## Common Log Patterns and Solutions

| Log Pattern | Likely Issue | Recovery Approach |
|-------------|--------------|-------------------|
| "Cannot read property 'X' of undefined" | Null reference | Add null checks and validation |
| "Cannot set property 'X' of undefined" | State update on unmounted component | Track component mount status |
| "Maximum update depth exceeded" | Infinite update loop | Fix useEffect dependency array |
| "Unhandled promise rejection" | Missing catch handler | Add proper promise error handling |
| "Slow render detected" | Performance bottleneck | Add memoization and rendering optimization |
| "API request failed" | Network or endpoint issue | Enhance error handling and retry logic |
| "Excessive re-renders" | Component re-rendering too often | Fix dependency arrays and add memo |

## Enhanced Logging Implementation

For effective log-based recovery, implement a structured logging system:

```typescript
// Create logging utility
const createLogger = (componentName) => {
  const prefix = `[${componentName}]`;
  
  return {
    log: (message, data) => console.log(`${prefix} ${message}`, data || ''),
    warn: (message, data) => console.warn(`${prefix} ${message}`, data || ''),
    error: (message, data) => console.error(`${prefix} ${message}`, data || ''),
    info: (message, data) => console.info(`${prefix} ${message}`, data || ''),
    time: (label) => console.time(`${prefix} ${label}`),
    timeEnd: (label) => console.timeEnd(`${prefix} ${label}`),
    
    // Performance logging
    renderStart: () => {
      const startTime = performance.now();
      return () => {
        const duration = performance.now() - startTime;
        console.log(`${prefix} Render completed in ${duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
        return duration;
      };
    },
    
    // API logging
    logApiRequest: (url, method, body) => {
      console.log(`${prefix} API Request: ${method} ${url}`, body ? { body } : '');
      const startTime = performance.now();
      
      return {
        success: (response) => {
          const duration = performance.now() - startTime;
          console.log(`${prefix} API Success: ${method} ${url} in ${duration.toFixed(2)}ms`, response);
        },
        error: (error) => {
          const duration = performance.now() - startTime;
          console.error(`${prefix} API Error: ${method} ${url} in ${duration.toFixed(2)}ms`, error);
        }
      };
    }
  };
};

// Usage in component
const MyComponent = () => {
  const logger = createLogger('MyComponent');
  
  useEffect(() => {
    logger.log('Component mounted');
    return () => logger.log('Component unmounted');
  }, []);
  
  const fetchData = async () => {
    const apiLogger = logger.logApiRequest('/api/data', 'GET');
    
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/api/data');
      const data = await response.json();
      apiLogger.success(data);
      return data;
    } catch (error) {
      apiLogger.error(error);
      throw error;
    }
  };
  
  // Performance tracking
  const endRender = logger.renderStart();
  // Component JSX
  const result = (/* component JSX */);
  endRender();
  
  return result;
};
```

